## SQ-EDL-01 | librarians: no Nock Enough Arrows enchantments in trades
@group A
@commands Boot; `logs/latest.log`
@pass `enders_additions` and `ends_delight.ce.mixins.json` load; no missing model / texture for `endersdelight:` plants; no script error in `ends_delight/*.js`, `endersdelight/*.js`; wild-crops log lists the 5 End rules (EDL-16)
@fails
@from batches/r1101/w2_worldgen.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@superseded duplicate of SQ-ENC-01 (rows/SSP.qb, same librarian NEA steps; the 2026-11-17 EN -> EDL/ENC prefix rename left this copy under EDL, its @pass cell is End's Delight EDL-01 text) (owner request, 2026-11-20)
> forceload add -16 -16 16 16
> setblock 2 100 2 minecraft:lectern
> summon minecraft:villager 2 101 3 {VillagerData:{profession:"minecraft:librarian",level:1,type:"minecraft:plains"},NoAI:1b,Tags:["en1"]}
> data get entity @e[tag=en1,limit=1] Offers
> data merge entity @e[tag=en1,limit=1] {VillagerData:{level:5},Offers:{}}
sleep 2
> data get entity @e[tag=en1,limit=1] Offers
> dumptrades
sleep 5
reject nock_enough_arrows:(stockpile|recovery|cycle)
shell ! grep -rqE "nock_enough_arrows:(stockpile|recovery|cycle)" kubejs/exported/villager_trades.json
look librarians offer enchanted books; Offers reset at a level change may need a trade-up; record what the level-5 librarian offered

## SQ-EDL-02 | Lightman's Currency cashiers: no NEA enchantments
@group A
@commands `/dumptrades` on the server; read the `lightmanscurrency:cashier` profession in the server's `kubejs/exported/villager_trades.json`
@pass the cashier profession is in the dump and none of its trades names `nock_enough_arrows:stockpile`, `recovery` or `cycle`
@fails NEA enchantments not removed from the book pools the cashier draws on
@from batches/r1101/w2_worldgen.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-20
@superseded duplicate of SQ-ENC-02 (rows/SSP.qb, same cashier check, which carries this fix; the 2026-11-17 EN -> EDL/ENC prefix rename left this copy under EDL) (owner request, 2026-11-20)
# r1120lr batch fault: the summoned cashier (y 101, no NoAI) was swapped by MCA (profession none) and fell to its death; the row now reads the profession's trade table from /dumptrades instead of a live villager's Offers
> dumptrades
sleep 5
shell python3 -c "import json,re,sys;d=json.load(open('kubejs/exported/villager_trades.json'));c=d['professions'].get('lightmanscurrency:cashier');print('cashier in dump:',c is not None);t=json.dumps(c);bad=re.findall(r'nock_enough_arrows:(?:stockpile|recovery|cycle)',t);print('NEA hits:',len(bad));sys.exit(1 if c is None or bad else 0)"
look the shell line: cashier in dump True, NEA hits 0; whether cashiers offer enchanted books at all is in the same dump

## SQ-EDL-03 | void pepper half: sprout count stays 1, origin fruits; fruiting sprout drops 3, plain sprout 1 (soils / growth passed in r1102b s3)
@group A
@commands Place the 4 plants on end stone, tilled end stone, dirt, farmland (EDL-03); random tick speed 100 on both soils (EDL-04, EDL-05)
@pass Only the two soils; faster on tilled; void pepper does not spread (sprout count stays 1) and the origin fruits, 3 / 1 drops
@fails
@from batches/r1103/p2_R.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-23
# no bot here any more (randomtick needs no player), so the lane is forceloaded instead
> forceload add 320 520 334 534
sleep 2
> fill 320 -61 520 334 -61 534 minecraft:end_stone
> fill 320 -60 520 334 -57 534 minecraft:air
> setblock 327 -60 527 endersdelight:voidpepper_block[down=true,spreading=true,pepper=false]
# 30 random ticks per block = the old 20 s at tick speed 300 near a bot (randomtick needs no player). Since 2026-11-23 the sprout no longer spreads: one tick passing the soil chance fruits it
> cdevtest randomtick 320 -60 520 334 -57 534 30
> cdevtest count 320 -60 520 334 -57 534 endersdelight:voidpepper_block
expect verb=count block=endersdelight:voidpepper_block n=1\b
> execute if block 327 -60 527 endersdelight:voidpepper_block[spreading=false,pepper=true] run say EN03 origin fruited
> execute unless block 327 -60 527 endersdelight:voidpepper_block[pepper=true] run say EN03 origin not fruited
> fill 320 -60 520 334 -57 534 minecraft:air
> setblock 322 -60 522 endersdelight:voidpepper_block[down=true,spreading=false,pepper=true]
> cdevtest break 322 -60 522
> setblock 324 -60 522 endersdelight:voidpepper_block[down=true,spreading=false,pepper=false]
> cdevtest break 324 -60 522
expect verb=break who=\S+ broken=true before="?endersdelight:voidpepper_block\S* after=minecraft:air
expect verb=break drops=endersdelight:voidpepper:3 stacks=\d+\b
expect verb=break drops=endersdelight:voidpepper:1 stacks=1\b
> forceload remove 320 520 334 534
look the sprout count (exactly 1 after 30 random ticks per block; more than 1 means it still spreads) and the origin line ("EN03 origin fruited" printed, "origin not fruited" is a fail)
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ .*error=

